WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

NOTE Descriptive captions for a silent animation. Timings match wilkes_basin_bed_reveal_animation_web.mp4 (27.3 s). Vertical exaggeration 100x.

00:00.000 --> 00:02.100
The East Antarctic Ice Sheet over the Wilkes
Subglacial Basin. Purple to yellow lines
show ice flow speed (20–500 m per year).

00:02.100 --> 00:05.600
Flying in to the Ninnis and Cook ice fronts.

00:05.600 --> 00:07.700
Outlet glaciers cross the grounding line
and float as ice shelves.

00:07.700 --> 00:12.600
Pulling back to the regional view.

00:12.600 --> 00:16.800
The ice sheet lifts off its bed.
Bedrock appears beneath: blue below
sea level, green and brown above.

00:16.800 --> 00:19.600
Ice flow lines freeze in place
as the ice is removed.

00:19.600 --> 00:23.800
Zooming to the basin floor, hundreds
of metres below sea level.

00:23.800 --> 00:27.300
Wilkes Subglacial Basin: a deep marine basin
under the East Antarctic Ice Sheet.
